{
  "notes": "Chillwave from a stretched cassette, Bb major, 82 BPM, swung sixteenths. A vocal pad (VOICE SOUL OOH) holds rootless seventh chords that the kick pumps once the drums arrive, a round sine bass (ANALOG SUB BASS) on roots and fifths, the player's soft gliding lead on the Smart Keys (ANALOG G-FUNK LD with a slow vibrato), and the VINTAGE rhythm box (CR-78 style) with a swung shaker. The tape: hiss and crackle (DUST), slow deep chorus wow, a dark triplet echo, a soft room. Scenes: A (SIDE A) plays Imaj7 to iii7; B steps down IVmaj7 iii7 ii7 Imaj7; C climbs IVmaj7 V vi7 Imaj7 with four kicks and a clap; D (SIDE B) floats on iii7 and IVmaj7. ENERGY: the pad alone, unpumped, then kick, bass and the pump, then snare, clap and hats, then the swung shaker, open hats, ratchets and fills. All material is original.",
